{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "washtenaw-project-grades",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.60: the PROJECT-domain input database of `project-grades` (runspecs/), over `onroad/default-database.esm` like `inputs/washtenaw-project.esm`, whose description says what a domain document declares and why only that.\n\nmoves.rs builds it from `characterization/county-inputs/washtenaw-project-grades/setup-project-grades.sql`: `washtenaw-project-links`' SQL with five on-network links of four grades, one above every drive schedule of its road type and one below source type 21's, which tools/build-scale-input-db.py writes to `inputs/washtenaw-project-grades/`. No user operating modes.\n\nIT DOES NOT LOAD ALONE: it names no runspec.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "onroad",
      "domain",
      "project-domain",
      "scale-input-database"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_link": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/Link.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_link"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "output",
          "domain"
        ],
        "note": "The project's Link: 5 rows in county 26161, zone 261610 -- links 1, 2 and 4 on road type 4 (1.0 mi at 30 mph grade 0; 0.8 mi at 30 mph grade 4; 1.2 mi at 80 mph grade 0, above every schedule), links 3 and 5 on road type 5 (0.5 mi at 25 mph grade -3; 0.2 mi at 2 mph grade 1.5, below source type 21's slowest schedule). Links 2, 4 and 5 are the locations after the run's two road types (`n_projectExtraLinks` 3), and the four grades are the link chain's four slots (`n_projectGrade` 4).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_linksourcetypehour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/linkSourceTypeHour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_linksourcetypehour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "10 rows: links 1-5 are 80/20, 70/30, 60/40, 90/10 and 50/50 percent source types 21 and 62.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_offnetworklink": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/offNetworkLink.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_offnetworklink"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "2 rows in zone 261610: 1,000 passenger cars and 50 long-haul trucks. The run selects no off-network road type, so nothing reads them.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_opmodedistribution": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/OpModeDistribution.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_opmodedistribution"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "operating-mode"
        ],
        "note": "0 rows: the user states no operating modes, so LinkOperatingModeDistributionGenerator computes every link's.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_driveschedulesecondlink": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/driveScheduleSecondLink.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_driveschedulesecondlink"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "operating-mode"
        ],
        "note": "0 rows: created EMPTY on purpose, so that LinkOperatingModeDistributionGenerator takes the average-speed path (step 105) on every link rather than walking a user schedule (step 100's first arm). `run_userLinkSchedules` counts the rows it would walk.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecdomain": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/runspecdomain.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecdomain"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "domain"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, modelDomain PROJECT, read by tools/build-scale-input-db.py from project-grades.xml.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_input_zoneroadtype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/ZoneRoadType.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_inputzoneroadtype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "The project's ZoneRoadType: 4 rows, the default's at zone 261610 (tools/build-scale-input-db.py --copy), as in `washtenaw-project`.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_input_hotellingactivitydistribution": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/hotellingActivityDistribution.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_inputhotellingactivitydistribution"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "hotelling"
        ],
        "note": "The project's hotellingActivityDistribution: 0 rows -- its copy selects zone 261610 from a default table whose rows are all at 990000. In PROJECT domain MOVES does not merge the default's at all (InputDataManager.java:2802-2805), which the model writes as `had_isMerged`.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_hotellinghoursperday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/hotellingHoursPerDay.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hotellinghoursperday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "hotelling"
        ],
        "note": "The project's hotellingHoursPerDay: 0 rows, a copy of the default's empty table.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_hotellinghourfraction": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/hotellingHourFraction.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hotellinghourfraction"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "hotelling"
        ],
        "note": "The project's hotellingHourFraction: 0 rows, a copy of the default's empty table.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_hotellingagefraction": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/hotellingAgeFraction.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hotellingagefraction"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "hotelling"
        ],
        "note": "The project's hotellingAgeFraction: 0 rows, a copy of the default's empty table.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_hotellingmonthadjust": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/hotellingMonthAdjust.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hotellingmonthadjust"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "hotelling"
        ],
        "note": "The project's hotellingMonthAdjust: 0 rows, a copy of the default's empty table.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_idlemodelyeargrouping": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../movesdb/idleModelYearGrouping.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_idlemodelyeargrouping"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "idleModelYearGrouping, the default database's: 0 rows, which the project database copies. Off-network idle is not computed in PROJECT domain, so nothing reads it there. AdjustTotalIdleFraction.sql's input (`oni_totalIdleFraction`): any `idleModelYearGrouping` row at a selected source type REPLACES `totalIdleFraction`, and `idleMonthAdjust` / `idleDayAdjust` scale the fraction at the rows their keys find. The default database's side is empty, so the domain states the merged table whole, as it does the hotelling adjustment tables.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_idlemonthadjust": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../movesdb/idleMonthAdjust.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_idlemonthadjust"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "idleMonthAdjust, the default database's: 0 rows, which the project database copies. Off-network idle is not computed in PROJECT domain, so nothing reads it there. AdjustTotalIdleFraction.sql's input (`oni_totalIdleFraction`): any `idleModelYearGrouping` row at a selected source type REPLACES `totalIdleFraction`, and `idleMonthAdjust` / `idleDayAdjust` scale the fraction at the rows their keys find. The default database's side is empty, so the domain states the merged table whole, as it does the hotelling adjustment tables.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_idledayadjust": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../movesdb/idleDayAdjust.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_idledayadjust"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "idleDayAdjust, the default database's: 0 rows, which the project database copies. Off-network idle is not computed in PROJECT domain, so nothing reads it there. AdjustTotalIdleFraction.sql's input (`oni_totalIdleFraction`): any `idleModelYearGrouping` row at a selected source type REPLACES `totalIdleFraction`, and `idleMonthAdjust` / `idleDayAdjust` scale the fraction at the rows their keys find. The default database's side is empty, so the domain states the merged table whole, as it does the hotelling adjustment tables.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_startsperday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/startsPerDay.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_startsperday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "starts"
        ],
        "note": "The project's startsPerDay: 0 rows, a copy of the default's empty table.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_input_zone": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-project-grades/Zone.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_inputzone"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "starts"
        ],
        "note": "The project's Zone: 1 row, setup-project.sql's copy of the default's zone 261610 (tools/build-scale-input-db.py --copy). The input side of a row merge with the default's, so the merged value is the default's own.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    }
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "n_outputRate": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 375,
      "description": "How many (pollutant-process, cohort) PAIRS reach MOVESOutput, summed over the run's emitted blocks. Declared here as well as in the model it mounts for the reason the numbers around it are (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1): this is the relay that lets a per-fixture document set it. It replaces `n_outputCohort` and `n_outputPolProcess`, which between them could describe only a rectangle. 375 is `process-tirewear`'s, three blocks of 125; a run with one emitted block of 125 needs 125, `expand-fueltype-diesel` 248, `expand-sourcetype` 430 and `expand-criteria` 372. `rateSurvivorCount` recomputes it, so it is a CHECKED declaration."
    },
    "n_sourceBin": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "How many source bins the widest cohort of the run holds. Declared here as well as in the model it mounts for the reason the two numbers above it are (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1): this is the relay that lets a per-fixture document set it. 1 is right for a run whose cohorts are single-binned -- a passenger car's are, and so the bin relation is that run's cohort relation row for row -- and a run that selects a light commercial truck needs 2, a refuse truck 8. `run_sourceBinsDropped` recomputes whether the value is enough, so it is a CHECKED declaration."
    },
    "n_physicsRow": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "How many rows of `sourceusetypephysics` the run's source types select between them -- the width of the drive-cycle axis. Declared here as well as in the model it mounts for the reason the three numbers above it are (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1): this is the relay that lets a per-fixture document set it. The vehicle a drive cycle is computed for is keyed by (sourceTypeID, regClassID, model-year range), so 1 is right for a motorcycle or a passenger car, a light commercial truck alone needs 3, source types 21 and 32 together 4, and the five of `expand-sourcetype` 40. `run_physicsRowsSelected` recomputes it and `run_physicsRowsDropped` says whether it is enough, so it is a CHECKED declaration."
    },
    "n_ratesScale": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "The RunSpec's `<modelscale>`: 1 at Rates scale, 0 (the default) at inventory scale. Relayed here as `n_outputRate` is (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1), so a per-fixture document can bind it (PLAN.md §7.3.47)."
    },
    "n_outputSumsDays": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "THE RUNSPEC'S `<outputtimestep>`, first half: 1 when it is `Month` or `Year`, whose MOVESOutput sums every (day type, hour) cell of a month and scales it by the month's weeks (AggregationSQLGenerator's convertWeeks, `noOfDays/7`); 0 (the default) at `Hour`. Relayed here as `n_outputRate` is (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1), so a per-fixture document can bind it (PLAN.md §7.3.63)."
    },
    "n_outputSumsMonths": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "THE RUNSPEC'S `<outputtimestep>`, second half: 1 when it is `Year`, whose MOVESOutput also sums the months; 0 (the default) otherwise. Relayed here as `n_outputRate` is (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1), so a per-fixture document can bind it (PLAN.md §7.3.63)."
    },
    "n_outputSumsHours": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "THE RUNSPEC'S `<outputtimestep>`, `requiresAllHours`: 1 at `24-Hour Day` and `Portion of Week`, whose MOVESOutput sums each day type's hours; 0 (the default) otherwise. Relayed here as `n_outputRate` is (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1), so a per-fixture document can bind it (PLAN.md §7.3.66)."
    },
    "n_outputClassicalDay": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "THE RUNSPEC'S `<outputtimestep>`, `usesClassicalDay`: 1 (the default) at `Hour` and `24-Hour Day`, 0 at `Portion of Week`, whose rows are a portion of a week rather than a classical day. Relayed here as `n_outputRate` is (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1), so a per-fixture document can bind it (PLAN.md §7.3.66)."
    },
    "n_projectExtraLinks": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "How many selected project links share a (county, road type) with an earlier link -- the locations after the run's selected road types. Relayed here as `n_outputRate` is (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1), so a per-fixture document can bind it; the model checks it (`run_extraLinksUndeclared`, PLAN.md §7.3.60)."
    },
    "n_projectGrade": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "How many distinct grades the run's on-network project links have -- the width of the link chain's grade axis. Relayed here as `n_outputRate` is (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1), so a per-fixture document can bind it; the model checks it (`run_gradesUndeclared`, PLAN.md §7.3.60)."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "Onroad": {
      "ref": "../onroad/default-database.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "n_outputRate": "n_outputRate",
        "n_sourceBin": "n_sourceBin",
        "n_physicsRow": "n_physicsRow",
        "n_ratesScale": "n_ratesScale",
        "n_outputSumsDays": "n_outputSumsDays",
        "n_outputSumsMonths": "n_outputSumsMonths",
        "n_outputSumsHours": "n_outputSumsHours",
        "n_outputClassicalDay": "n_outputClassicalDay",
        "n_projectExtraLinks": "n_projectExtraLinks",
        "n_projectGrade": "n_projectGrade"
      }
    }
  }
}
